      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start but i need to be able to justify these rankings to my stakeholders. \n\nfor the \"unstable\" or \"less aligned\" categories—specifically the Trap/Drill/AAVE cluster and the Reggaeton/Spanglish cluster—can you be more specific about the \"risk\" they pose? like, if a luxury brand accidentally adopts too much of that \"street\" or \"urban\" energy, what is the specific negative perception they face from high-net-worth clients? \n\nis it just about \"taste,\" or is there a deeper perception that these specific cultures are associated with higher crime rates, lower educational levels, or general social volatility? my clients need to know if there's a \"reputational danger\" in being seen as even remotely connected to those demographics.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
